**RCA summary:**
- Bug: A validating PR whose dispatched validation run concluded `cancelled` (or whose dispatch was lost) keeps the `ai_validating` arm forever — the arm holds the serial merge-window mutex while no live run exists behind it, starving the whole merge window.
- Root cause: `sweep_stale_validation` in `js/smAgent.js` (the stale-arm sweeper) only sweeps CONCLUDED verdicts (success/failure); `CANCELLED is never a verdict` → `!sOld` → "no concluded-and-stale validation run on the head — arm stays" and `continue`. A cancelled-only (or no-run) head therefore never re-dispatches and never unarms; `validate-armed`'s mutex scan (`js/sm/sources/githubSource.js` `q.mutex`) defers every other approved candidate for as long as the dead arm sits there. Live: fa PR #1443, 2026-10-09 13:36–15:00Z — arm held ~2h, 4 validated PRs deferred, manual `gh workflow run ci.yml` unstick.
- Impact: any single cancelled/lost dispatch on an armed head freezes the serial validation slot (and, for an approved arm, the whole merge window) until a human intervenes.
- Fix approach: liveness state machine in the sweep — classify the head's dispatched-run state (running / green / red / zombie-cancelled / zombie-no-run); zombie ⇒ bounded same-tick re-dispatch (1 per head per hour, marker-comment bookkeeping like the red-head markers) + release/re-acquire of the mutex slot; 3 zombie re-dispatches on the same head ⇒ `validation_failed` park + comment (fail-closed).

